WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.501 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So happy to have you here.
Congrats.

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:02.302 line:92%
This is really an accomplishment

00:00:02.302 --> 00:00:04.671 align:start size:94% position:6%
for the first time
you directed and wrote a film.

00:00:04.671 --> 00:00:05.538 size:81% position:41% line:92%
It's a beautiful film.

00:00:05.538 --> 00:00:06.439 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thanks.
Thanks for having me.

00:00:06.439 --> 00:00:08.775
-Were you --
At what point of being an actor

00:00:08.775 --> 00:00:11.511
did you think to yourself, "Oh,
I want to direct one of these,"

00:00:11.511 --> 00:00:12.912 align:start size:94% position:6%
or "I want to
write one of these?"

00:00:12.912 --> 00:00:17.050 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I have a very odd life,
because I started off

00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:18.852
wanting to be a writer/director
my whole life,

00:00:18.852 --> 00:00:22.022 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then I kind of
accidentally fell into

00:00:22.022 --> 00:00:24.524 align:start size:94% position:6%
this amazing
16-year acting career,

00:00:24.524 --> 00:00:26.860 align:start size:94% position:6%
which has been
an insane journey

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:28.495 align:start size:94% position:6%
and is an insane journey,
as well.

00:00:28.495 --> 00:00:31.631 align:start size:94% position:6%
But it took me a long time
to figure out --

00:00:31.631 --> 00:00:34.401
I hold the position of director
in such high regard

00:00:34.401 --> 00:00:37.037 align:start size:94% position:6%
that I didn't want
to just be some actor

00:00:37.037 --> 00:00:38.538 line:92%
goofing off trying to do it.

00:00:38.538 --> 00:00:40.306 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's something
that matters to me,

00:00:40.306 --> 00:00:41.608 align:start size:94% position:6%
something that's
important to me,

00:00:41.608 --> 00:00:44.978
and so I took four years,
and I waited till I had a story

00:00:44.978 --> 00:00:46.613 align:start size:94% position:6%
that rally
meant something to me.

00:00:46.613 --> 00:00:47.447 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-It's called "Mid90s."

00:00:47.447 --> 00:00:49.749 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's about a group of kids
in the mid '90s.

00:00:49.749 --> 00:00:52.252 size:81% position:41%
They're skateboarders.
That is the culture.

00:00:52.252 --> 00:00:55.455 align:start size:94% position:6%
I have to assume that you were
pulling for something

00:00:55.455 --> 00:00:57.524 align:start size:94% position:6%
from your own life
because of the amount

00:00:57.524 --> 00:00:59.225 line:92%
of specificity to this world.

00:00:59.225 --> 00:01:00.360 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, this had
to have been something

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:02.328 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you experienced
to some degree.

00:01:02.328 --> 00:01:03.296 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-Yeah, I mean, I was

00:01:03.296 --> 00:01:05.999 align:start size:94% position:6%
a horrifically
terrible skateboarder.

00:01:05.999 --> 00:01:07.233 align:start size:94% position:6%
I -- I --
[ Laughter ]

00:01:07.233 --> 00:01:10.937
I would film, 'cause I liked
to tell people what to do,

00:01:10.937 --> 00:01:11.771 line:92%
and I wanted to be a director.

00:01:11.771 --> 00:01:15.075
So it was the perfect role
in that group of friends.

00:01:15.075 --> 00:01:17.710 line:92%
And I was unathletic, so...

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:18.978 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:18.978 --> 00:01:22.148 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, you know,
the story's about --

00:01:22.148 --> 00:01:26.119 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's not a biopic,
but it's personal in the sense

00:01:26.119 --> 00:01:31.491
that I relate to being 13,
I relate to being lonely,

00:01:31.491 --> 00:01:33.259 line:92%
and I relate to something

00:01:33.259 --> 00:01:36.696 size:81% position:41%
giving you a community
outside of your home

00:01:36.696 --> 00:01:37.697 size:81% position:41% line:92%
and a group of friends

00:01:37.697 --> 00:01:39.032 align:start size:94% position:6%
and something
to fall in love with.

00:01:39.032 --> 00:01:41.534 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, ultimately,
this movie is just about

00:01:41.534 --> 00:01:43.303 line:92%
a group of kids at a time

00:01:43.303 --> 00:01:44.804 align:start size:94% position:6%
when it's you and your friends
versus the world

00:01:44.804 --> 00:01:47.740 align:start size:94% position:6%
and your family is less
important than your friends.

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:50.844
-I've heard you refer to it
as an animal-kingdom movie.

00:01:50.844 --> 00:01:53.513 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'm assuming that refers
to just the pecking order

00:01:53.513 --> 00:01:57.250
of kids at that age and how some
are more dominant than others.

00:01:57.250 --> 00:01:59.819
-Yeah, well, the kid's like 13,
and then there's another kid

00:01:59.819 --> 00:02:03.523
who's like 14 who kind of is
the first one that talks to him,

00:02:03.523 --> 00:02:05.725 size:78% position:39%
and then there's kids
up to like 18, 19.

00:02:05.725 --> 00:02:08.528 align:start size:94% position:6%
So he's kind of figuring out
how to play --

00:02:08.528 --> 00:02:13.900
move around the chessboard
and figure out how to fit in

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:14.934 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
and then move up.

00:02:14.934 --> 00:02:18.371 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I don't know.
It's just -- I've related --

00:02:18.371 --> 00:02:21.808
I kind of feel like all of
the characters in some ways,

00:02:21.808 --> 00:02:25.612 size:75% position:38%
because I feel like,
when you're young,

00:02:25.612 --> 00:02:26.513 line:92%
in the '90s especially --

00:02:26.513 --> 00:02:27.714 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know
if you relate to this.

00:02:27.714 --> 00:02:28.848 align:start size:94% position:6%
A big part
of the movie is, like,

00:02:28.848 --> 00:02:34.287
the corniest thing you could do
is try or care about anything.

00:02:34.287 --> 00:02:35.788 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that's
a big part of the movie

00:02:35.788 --> 00:02:36.556 line:92%
is that none of them care,

00:02:36.556 --> 00:02:38.391 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it's kind of showing off
how little they care.

00:02:38.391 --> 00:02:41.161 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, they're pretty much
beautiful morons

00:02:41.161 --> 00:02:43.696 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, essentially,
like my friends and I were.

00:02:43.696 --> 00:02:44.497 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know?
Which is like,

00:02:44.497 --> 00:02:48.768 align:start size:94% position:6%
they make so many mistakes,
they speak in ugly vernacular,

00:02:48.768 --> 00:02:52.305 align:start size:94% position:6%
there's toxic masculinity,
homophobia,

00:02:52.305 --> 00:02:53.873 align:start size:94% position:6%
things that are true
to the time

00:02:53.873 --> 00:02:55.241 size:84% position:42% line:92%
and truly hard to watch

00:02:55.241 --> 00:03:00.246
but I felt would be more
offensive to be revisionist

00:03:00.246 --> 00:03:01.414 line:92%
and to change the way it was

00:03:01.414 --> 00:03:03.716 size:81% position:41%
than to hold a mirror
up to how ugly it was.

00:03:03.716 --> 00:03:06.753
So these kids do things,
they endanger each other's live,

00:03:06.753 --> 00:03:09.656 align:start size:94% position:6%
but at the same time,
they deeply love each other.

00:03:09.656 --> 00:03:11.558 align:start size:94% position:6%
So nothing's
really black-and-white,

00:03:11.558 --> 00:03:12.625 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the movie's
not black-and-white,

00:03:12.625 --> 00:03:15.228
and I hope, if I'm lucky enough
to get to do this again,

00:03:15.228 --> 00:03:18.231 align:start size:94% position:6%
to always create
complex characters

00:03:18.231 --> 00:03:22.101
that are challenging what our
definitions of good and bad are.

00:03:22.101 --> 00:03:24.771 align:start size:94% position:6%
-One thing that's amazing is,
no matter how good

00:03:24.771 --> 00:03:26.873 align:start size:94% position:6%
a script you wrote
or how well you directed it,

00:03:26.873 --> 00:03:28.608 align:start size:94% position:6%
obviously, it was
very reliant on the cast,

00:03:28.608 --> 00:03:33.246
and you went outside of just
natural professional actors,

00:03:33.246 --> 00:03:35.281 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you cast
a lot of skateboarders

00:03:35.281 --> 00:03:36.249 line:92%
to be the actors in this film.

00:03:36.249 --> 00:03:38.284 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, and I actually
wanted to finish my point,

00:03:38.284 --> 00:03:40.687 align:start size:94% position:6%
because I went astray
for one moment,

00:03:40.687 --> 00:03:41.387 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
which is just --

00:03:41.387 --> 00:03:43.089 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that's totally on me,
by the way.

00:03:43.089 --> 00:03:44.591 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, no.
-Not on you.

00:03:44.591 --> 00:03:45.291 size:75% position:38% line:92%
But the idea is that

00:03:45.291 --> 00:03:47.126
the corniest thing you could do
was to care.

00:03:47.126 --> 00:03:49.495 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And there's a kid

00:03:49.495 --> 00:03:51.598 size:84% position:42%
named Ray in the movie,
a character named Ray,

00:03:51.598 --> 00:03:55.235
who's played beautifully
by one of the first-time actors,

00:03:55.235 --> 00:03:55.868 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Na-kel Smith.

00:03:55.868 --> 00:04:03.109 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he tells this kid,
in a way that's not corny,

00:04:03.109 --> 00:04:06.446 align:start size:94% position:6%
and subtly, basically,
he does care

00:04:06.446 --> 00:04:07.680 size:88% position:44% line:92%
and he's trying at life.

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:10.083 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I found,
whether I was a young kid

00:04:10.083 --> 00:04:11.351 line:92%
trying to fit into a group

00:04:11.351 --> 00:04:12.752 align:start size:94% position:6%
or the older kid
trying to make

00:04:12.752 --> 00:04:14.621 align:start size:94% position:6%
someone else
kind of care a little bit,

00:04:14.621 --> 00:04:18.758
when someone older takes the
moment to show you something

00:04:18.758 --> 00:04:20.426 line:92%
in a non-corny, sweaty way,

00:04:20.426 --> 00:04:22.795 align:start size:94% position:6%
it sticks with you
for the rest of your life.

00:04:22.795 --> 00:04:23.863 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-You know?

00:04:23.863 --> 00:04:26.699 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's really
a very moving story

00:04:26.699 --> 00:04:28.167 align:start size:94% position:6%
even if, at times,
it's hard to watch,

00:04:28.167 --> 00:04:30.103 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it's funny,
and it's crazy.

00:04:30.103 --> 00:04:30.770 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-It's really funny.

00:04:30.770 --> 00:04:32.972 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I can't believe
that they weren't actors.

00:04:32.972 --> 00:04:34.407 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, like --
And you tell --

00:04:34.407 --> 00:04:36.409 align:start size:94% position:6%
By the way, I know --
-They are now.

00:04:36.409 --> 00:04:37.310 align:start size:94% position:6%
-They are now.
-Yeah.

00:04:37.310 --> 00:04:39.345
-I know actors, and once
they started skateboarding,

00:04:39.345 --> 00:04:42.115
I'm like, "Oh, that's not actors
who learned how to skateboard.

00:04:42.115 --> 00:04:43.516 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is definitely
the other way around."

00:04:43.516 --> 00:04:46.352 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, I did, basically,
everything to make

00:04:46.352 --> 00:04:48.688 align:start size:94% position:6%
this incredibly difficult
for myself.

00:04:48.688 --> 00:04:50.290 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Uh-huh.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:50.290 --> 00:04:51.491 line:92%
-My lead was 11 years old.

00:04:51.491 --> 00:04:52.825 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're not supposed
to work with children.

00:04:52.825 --> 00:04:55.495 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Who's fantastic.
-Sunny Suljic, he's brilliant.

00:04:55.495 --> 00:04:58.097 size:78% position:39%
The rest of the cast,
besides his family,

00:04:58.097 --> 00:04:59.799 align:start size:94% position:6%
played by Katherine Waterston
and Lucas Hedges,

00:04:59.799 --> 00:05:03.770 size:81% position:41%
both brilliant actors,
are first-time actors,

00:05:03.770 --> 00:05:04.937 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they're all
real skateboarders.

00:05:04.937 --> 00:05:08.574
A lot of them are professionals,
you know, or semiprofessional,

00:05:08.574 --> 00:05:10.376 line:92%
and, you know, skateboarding,

00:05:10.376 --> 00:05:13.179 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is always constantly
butchered in film.

00:05:13.179 --> 00:05:16.816
So, I chose a subculture that
doesn't want to be spoken about

00:05:16.816 --> 00:05:18.551 align:start size:94% position:6%
and doesn't want the kid
from "Superbad"

00:05:18.551 --> 00:05:19.952 line:92%
making a movie about them.

00:05:19.952 --> 00:05:21.654 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:21.654 --> 00:05:23.589 align:start size:94% position:6%
I chose to work with children,
which are --

00:05:23.589 --> 00:05:26.426
Notoriously, you're not supposed
work with children or animals.

00:05:26.426 --> 00:05:31.130 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I also decided
to take on the duty

00:05:31.130 --> 00:05:33.032 line:92%
of elegantly framing hip-hop,

00:05:33.032 --> 00:05:36.402 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is another subculture
often butchered on film

00:05:36.402 --> 00:05:38.171 align:start size:94% position:6%
that doesn't want
the kid from "Superbad"

00:05:38.171 --> 00:05:39.739 size:88% position:44% line:92%
making a movie about it,

00:05:39.739 --> 00:05:42.141 align:start size:94% position:6%
about how this music
is the emotional backbone

00:05:42.141 --> 00:05:44.043 align:start size:94% position:6%
of my and a lot
of people's childhood

00:05:44.043 --> 00:05:47.013 align:start size:94% position:6%
and how A Tribe Called Quest
is, to me,

00:05:47.013 --> 00:05:50.083 align:start size:94% position:6%
what John Lennon
is to my parents.

00:05:50.083 --> 00:05:50.783 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Right?

00:05:50.783 --> 00:05:54.120 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I guess
I'm comfortable in discomfort

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:55.788 align:start size:94% position:6%
and comfortable
with a lot of challenges

00:05:55.788 --> 00:06:01.361
because it turned out to be
the most beautiful, challenging,

00:06:01.361 --> 00:06:04.664 size:81% position:41%
emotional, incredible
experience of my life.

00:06:04.664 --> 00:06:06.065 size:78% position:39% line:92%
And I am genuinely --

00:06:06.065 --> 00:06:07.800 align:start size:94% position:6%
I have to come on here
and sell [bleep]

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:09.068 line:92%
whether I like it or not.

00:06:09.068 --> 00:06:09.869 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:06:09.869 --> 00:06:10.603 size:84% position:42% line:92%
I'm being dead serious.

00:06:10.603 --> 00:06:12.105
I could be on here next time,
like, telling you something...

00:06:12.105 --> 00:06:15.208 size:78% position:39%
-Wait! Wait a second!
You've lied to me?!

00:06:15.208 --> 00:06:16.976 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I love seeing you.

00:06:16.976 --> 00:06:18.878 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:18.878 --> 00:06:20.580 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I love seeing you.

00:06:20.580 --> 00:06:22.882 size:81% position:41%
And I love seeing you,
and I love seeing you,

00:06:22.882 --> 00:06:23.716 line:92%
and I love seeing all of you,

00:06:23.716 --> 00:06:26.786
and sometimes I have to be
on here on some bull [bleep]

00:06:26.786 --> 00:06:31.290 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, like,
this movie is my heart.

00:06:31.290 --> 00:06:33.826 line:92%
I spent four years making it.

00:06:33.826 --> 00:06:34.394 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I care about it.

00:06:34.394 --> 00:06:37.029 align:start size:94% position:6%
I love it, and I promise you,
if you go see it,

00:06:37.029 --> 00:06:40.233 align:start size:94% position:6%
you will be moved and laugh
and enjoy yourself.

00:06:40.233 --> 00:06:42.769 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, thank you.
Go see it.

